   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to the women veterans\ncoordinator",
    "basePrintNo": "S5991",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5991-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 38,
       "fullName": "David Carlucci",
       "imgName": "370_david_carlucci.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 370,
       "sessionMemberId": 1191,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "CARLUCCI"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §361-b, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5991\n \nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to the\nwomen veterans coordinator\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to clarify and update the duties of the\nwomen veterans coordinator within the New York State Division of Veter-\nans' Services.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Subdivision 1 of section 361-b of the executive law is, as\namended by chapter 515 of the laws of 2911, is amended to include new\nduties for the women veterans coordinator. They include:  advocating for\nall women veterans in the state; promoting events and activities that\nrecognize, education and honor women veterans including veteran human\nrights conferences, veterans benefits and resources events and veterans\ncultural competence trainings, including of the contributions women\nveterans have made on behalf of the United States and this state on the\ndivision's website and preparing reports on topics including but not\nlimited to demographics of women veterans, the number of women veterans\nlisted by county and the unique needs of the women veterans population.\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 271 of the laws of 1994, Chapter 358 of the laws of 1993 and\nChapter 515 of the laws of2011 were adopted in order to ensure that\nwomen veterans were part ofthe division of veterans' services by creat-\ning the position of a women veterans coordinator within the agency.\nThis bill updates the duties of the women veterans coordinator to\nreflect the many programs the division of veterans services carry out to\ncarry out its mission in serving the entire veterans community state-\nwide.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State or local governments.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\n",
